  "code_root_cause": {
    "file": "tools/cicflowmeter-java/src/main/java/cic/cs/unb/ca/jnetpcap/BasicFlow.java",
    "lines": "155, 196",
    "explanation": "In BasicFlow.java, Init_Win_bytes_forward is assigned once in the first-packet initialization block (line 141). In contrast, Init_Win_bytes_backward is set on line 155 for the first reverse packet, but is then repeatedly and unconditionally overwritten on line 196: 'Init_Win_bytes_backward = packet.getTCPWindow();' for every subsequent backward packet. On modern Linux TCP stacks with Window Scaling enabled (wscale=10), established data ACK packets carry an unscaled raw window field of 64 (which multiplies by 2^10 = 1024 to a true receive window of 65,536 bytes). Because Java CICFlowMeter does not parse TCP options and continually overwrites this field, the final reported Init_Win_bytes_backward is the raw 16-bit window of the last backward packet (64)."
  }
